// A container of a type parameter is admitted on its own, because it is
// wrapped whole and the wrapper carries the descriptor. Under a tuple there is
// no wrapper: a tuple is converted field by field, so this field would be
// converted too, and the only conversion for a container is the structural one
// this design exists to avoid. The two shapes are even the same size, so
// nothing downstream would refuse it.
//
// The call below reports F002 as well, because a signature that does not
// resolve leaves its function unregistered. That one used to be the only thing
// said, which named the symptom and left the reader to guess.
fun f<T>(x: ([T], u32)): u32
  ret x.1
end fun

let numbers: [u32] = [1]
let output = f((numbers, 2))
